lunchtime in the center of rio de  janeiro and workers at the soup kitchen  are busier than expected despite a  turnaround from the economic downturn  during the height of the covid19  pandemic  brazil is experiencing a surge in the  number of people living on the streets  we're facing a record 12 percent yearly  inflation which has doubled the price of  food in cooking gas many retirees have  lost their homes because they can no  longer survive on meager pensions even  young people who are back at work sleep  on the streets during the week because  they can't afford paying public  transportation every day and depend on  us for a free meal  in order to deal with the rising numbers  congress approved president bolsonaro's  plan to increase handouts for poor  brazilians with just three months to go  before the general election critics say  the measure is a scheme to boost his  re-election chances  polls show bolsonaro trailing behind  former president louisiana  brazilian legislation limits public  spending especially during an electoral  year but president bolsonaro was able to  bypass the ban by convincing congress to  declare a state of emergency until the  end of the year  antoino da silva is an unemployed car  mechanic he receives 74 dollars a month  from the government that handout will  increase to one hundred and ten dollars  in august  if bolsonaro thinks this will make me  vote for him he's wrong if he really  wanted to fight poverty he would have  invested in education health and jobs  instead of campaigning in favour of  arming the population with guns he  thinks he can trick us with emergency  aid which will only last until december  bolsonaro's allies justify the state of  emergency saying brazil's economy has  been hit hard by the war in ukraine  since the start of the war fuel prices  have increased  taxi and truck drivers will also receive  government handouts to fill up their  tanks  it's more of a political emergency than  an economic one bolsonaro will increase  the value and the number of handouts  until his first term is over then what  we've seen this film before and it does  not have a happy ending  during the pandemic government handouts  were also increased to 110  between march and august of 2020 the  number of poor people declined  dramatically from 65 million to 42  million helping bolsonaro's popularity  but once the emergency aid stopped in  january of 2021 poverty rates soared  today 75 million people in latin  america's largest economy live in  poverty manika yanaki of al jazeera rio  de janeiro
 

